# Credentials for these are already set on the skale-cron service
# (<PROJECT>_BASE_URL / <PROJECT>_CRON_SECRET), so enabling one is just
# uncommenting its line. URLs and cadences below were read from each repo's own
# workflow, not guessed.
#
# DO NOT simply uncomment and leave the GitHub schedule running. xphere can run
# both sides at once because its cron endpoints are idempotent by design. These
# are not known to be: two schedulers racing blog generation could publish the
# same post twice. Uncomment a line and delete that repo's `schedule:` block in
# the SAME change, once alerting is live.
